So stay tuned for that.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.300
Inspiration for today's video
I got on a conversation,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.980
that was going on on my Instagram Channel.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.150
In the last days I posted several pieces

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.670
of content on how you can actually handle

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.850
and address difficult
and sensitive situations,

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.700
that you might face in your work.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.830
And after that I received
messages from any

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.630
of you sharing situations
that you are facing

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.574
in your work environment

00:01:46.574 --> 00:01:48.510
or even also in your private life.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.000
And then we were having a discussion on,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.570
what you can actually do
in your specific instance.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:55.550
And adjust from it that
I like to share here

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.290
because I believe that many

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.680
of these problems are very much about,

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.090
how you actually confront
the other person,

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:04.830
and what ways of
communication you use in order

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.360
to make sure that you are
addressing the problems,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.193
in the right way.

00:02:08.193 --> 00:02:09.080
So as you can imagine,

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.570
there are many reasons
why in the workplace,

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:14.220
you might find yourself
in a sensitive situation.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.053
It could either be,

00:02:15.053 --> 00:02:17.300
that maybe you have an
argument with a client,

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.770
he might be unsatisfied,

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.870
with how you resolve a specific instance,

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.880
in your relationship.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.220
And there might be an issue,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.370
that you would like to solve.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.500
Or at least as likely
there might be a colleague

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.780
of yours whom you have
a disagreement with,

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.230
on a personal or work related topic.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.710
And now you're looking for a way

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:35.050
to resolve this kind of situation.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:36.550
Whenever there are people involved,

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.650
it's clear that there's
always a big potential,

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.350
for problems for drama
for sensitive situations.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.183
And the question is,

00:02:43.183 --> 00:02:45.450
how do you actually handle it?

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.283
And of course,

00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:48.770
this is not only true for
your professional life,

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:49.780
for your work life,

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.930
but at least as true for your private

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:52.800
and personal life.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.390
What I see many people
do in these situations

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.350
and this is also true for
many associates I work with,

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:00.690
when being a project lead.

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:03.780
People tend to like to write an email.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.200
Whenever there's a problem,

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.830
you write an email to send it

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:07.930
to the other person.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:09.750
And this is the way of communication,

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.200
that just many people choose.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.033
And there seem

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.150
to be some rather
obvious reasons for that.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:14.983
First of all,

00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:17.760
it's very often the easiest thing to do.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:18.670
Wherever you are,

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:19.900
whenever you have the time,

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.020
you can just write an email, send it off.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.570
And then from your perspective,

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.630
the problem is solved.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.290
At least this is what you think.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.630
And then second, also,

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.670
it helps you avoid
these tough discussions,

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:31.503
when you really need

00:03:31.503 --> 00:03:33.520
to look somebody in the face.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.700
And having this really hard,

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.680
to have face to face discussion,

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.330
with another person on a topic,

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.590
that might make you feel uncomfortable.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.980
On a topic where you
know that it's an issue,

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.150
for the other person,

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.200
that you just do not
know how to resolve this.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.840
People have a natural tendency

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.600
to avoid these kinds of
confrontation situations.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.170
And just writing an email often seems

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:57.200
to be an easy way out where you can avoid,

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.840
this direct confrontation
with your supervisors,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.240
with other colleagues,

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.470
with clients or with people
in your personal life.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:06.630
And many of the messages,

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.040
that you sent me on Instagram reminded me

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.070
of a prior instance,

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:12.550
when I was a young consultant at McKinsey.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:15.900
And I was facing such
a difficult situation,

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.520
with one of my clients
who I was responsible for.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.890
Now I already sent this
client several emails

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.510
and I was sitting in the TeamRoom

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.480
and complaining to my project lead saying,

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.570
this person is so difficult to work with.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.950
I've already sent him so many emails,

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.310
he just doesn't reply

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:33.340
or when he replies is
giving me such a bad time.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.550
I really do not know what else to do.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:36.770
And this was the moment,

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.950
where my project leader
that time taught me one

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:41.460
of the Golden Rules of consulting.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.600
How you interact with colleagues

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.720
and clients in this rule
are pretty much three words.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.410
It is walk, talk, write.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:55.780
Again, the rule is walk, talk, right?

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.760
What does it mean how is this rule

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:58.730
to be understood?

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.020
Well, it is a rule that is tell you,

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.130
how you should handle these kind

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.470
of difficult communication situations.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.440
And it gives you the priority,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.950
how you should act.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:12.820
The first priority that
you should follow is walk.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:13.653
And with walk,

00:05:13.653 --> 00:05:15.420
what is meant here is
that you are supposed

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:18.200
to walk to this person's desk,

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.560
walk through your clients,

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.010
to your colleagues desk,

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:24.550
and talk to the person face to face.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.610
Try to resolve the situation on a face

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:27.680
to face conversation.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.670
When you look somebody in the face,

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.800
you have the best opportunity

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.050
to really understand best the
other person's perspective

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.980
and come to an agreement that works,

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.670
for both sides on the table.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:39.590
And yes, of course,

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.300
it's not always possible to walk

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.390
to the other person

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:44.110
and then it might just not be feasible

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.580
to talk to the other person face to face.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:50.230
So the rule again goes, walk talk, write.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.350
So if walking is not possible,

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.810
then the second priority
for you is to talk.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.440
So this means that in this case,

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.910
you pick up the phone and you talk

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.240
to the person on the phone,

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.230
in order to resolve it.

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:04.370
And again, while it is a
significant difference,

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.670
whether you talk to the
person face to face,

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.880
or just on the phone,
talking on the phone,

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.520
or maybe on a video conference,

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.000
is the second best thing that you can do.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.880
And only if these things are not possible,

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.550
if they are not feasible,

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:18.720
then the third option is to write.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.100
Then you can open an email

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.180
and write whatever
thoughts you might have.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.040
Though here again, if you
write you might be smarter

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.470
to actually then just ask
for phone conversation

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.580
or for face to face meeting in order

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.550
to blowing out all your steam,

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:33.150
while writing it in an email, right?

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.400
So don't be an email warrior.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:36.590
This is what I mean here.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:38.300
If you need to write an email,

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.550
try to just use it to
have a phone conversation,

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:45.470
especially when the topics
are difficult and sensitive.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.690
And there's really a problem
that needs to be solved.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:49.680
If you just think about your experience.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.030
How there are you then
resolve the situations.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.010
I hope you agree with me that most

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.550
of the time it was due
to face to face meeting

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.850
or phone call and not just
by you writing an email.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.090
Even though of course,

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:03.520
I understand that in many situations,

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.590
it's just so much easier
to write an email than

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:08.260
to meet the person face to face.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.770
Especially if you know

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:11.940
and expect that the conversation is going

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:12.990
to be a difficult one.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.670
So looking back at that feedback point,

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:15.950
that I received as a young consultant,

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.640
for my project lead,

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:19.270
this was really a game changer.

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.720
This principle of walk talk, write,

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.100
really made a big difference,

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.270
in my professional life.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.620
And then when a few years later I advanced

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.360
to become a project lead myself,

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.910
when I had conversations
with my associates,

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:31.750
and they were telling me,

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.410
that they struggled in certain situations.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.760
That they struggled with
interacting with clients,

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:37.960
when then I try to understand,

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.310
how they have interacted
with them very often,

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:43.110
the result was that they
relied far too much,

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:44.550
on written communication.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:47.120
And just did not make an
effort big enough really,

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.610
to go out there and talk
to the people in person.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.300
So what are your experiences?

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:52.440
What do you think?

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.470
What difficult situations
have you already encountered,

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.760
